.TH JSFS 4
.SH NAME
jsfs \- JavaScript realms as files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jsfs
[
.B -D
] [
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Jsfs
serves JavaScript realms of the engine
(see
.IR js (1))
as files, by default at
.BR /mnt/js .
Each realm is a global object with its own built-ins, heap and jobs,
running on a process of its own: a script that runs long holds only
its realm, and
.B kill
ends it whatever it is doing.
.B -D
traces the Styx messages.
.SH FILESYSTEM
.TF N/console
.TP
.B clone
Reading it makes a realm and gives its number,
.IR N ,
and a newline.
.TP
.IB N /ctl
Reading gives
.BI "realm " N\f1.
Writing a line controls the realm:
.B kill
ends it and removes its directory;
.BI "stress " n
collects its garbage after every
.I n
allocations (0, as usual), to test the engine;
.BI "profile " ms
samples where it is every
.I ms
milliseconds (0 stops).
An unknown verb is an error.
.TP
.IB N /eval
Writing a script runs it; the write returns when it has run, and any
promise jobs it queued.
Reading gives the last script's value, as
.IR js (1)
prints it, or
.BI "error: " exception\f1.
Its mode is 600: it is authority to run code in the realm.
.TP
.IB N /console
What the realm's scripts printed
.RB ( print ,
.BR console.log ),
a line each; reads are by offset, and it grows.
.TP
.IB N /status
.B idle
or
.BR running ,
then
.BI "scripts " n\f1,
the number run, and
.BI "error " text
for the last that threw.
.TP
.IB N /profile
While profiling: where the time went, by function, a line each.
.PD
.PP
A realm cannot import modules: that would read files in the server's
namespace on a client's behalf.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
; n=`{cat /mnt/js/clone}
; echo '[1, 2, 3].map(x => x * 2)' > /mnt/js/$n/eval
; cat /mnt/js/$n/eval
2,4,6
; echo kill > /mnt/js/$n/ctl
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/jsfs.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/js
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR js (1),
.IR charon (1)
